  "prompt": "What conditions must a corporation satisfy to claim a bad debt as a deductible expense?",
  "runtimeCommit": "bd19b3d7a220132a618a3777a33fdfa0b34099ea",
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nTo claim a bad debt as a deductible expense, a corporation must demonstrate that the debt is considered worthless and that it has been previously included in gross income.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nIn practice, this means that corporations must maintain adequate records to substantiate the worthlessness of the debt and demonstrate that it was previously reported as income. This may involve providing documentation such as collection efforts, correspondence with the debtor, and any relevant financial statements. Proper documentation is crucial for the corporation to successfully claim the deduction during tax assessments.",
